package use_cases.actors;

/*
 * External actors for the HALCYON use cases.
 *
 * `actor def` is a top-level definition for an external participant — the
 * thing on the far side of a use-case boundary (an operator, a ground
 * station, an autonomous monitor). It parses exactly like `part def`
 * (KEYWORD "def" IDENT Body) and registers a type that `actor x : T`
 * usages resolve against.
 *
 * KerML mapping: KerML has no dedicated ActorDefinition metaclass — in
 * SysML v2 an actor is a part marked «actor». So `actor def` normalizes
 * (M1) to a KerML Structure / SysML PartDefinition (8.3.4.3.2) carrying an
 * «actor» MetadataFeature (8.3.4.12.3). Structure specializes Item in the
 * KerML hierarchy, so the «actor» marker rides on the item/part family
 * exactly as SysML v2 examples show. The `actor x : Operator` usages in the
 * use cases lower to PartUsage / KerML Feature (M1, 8.3.3.3.4) — the
 * load-bearing Feature mapping for every usage.
 */

/** A human operator: mission planner, ground controller. */
actor def Operator {
    public (
        attribute role : String [1];
        attribute organization : String [1] = "HALCYON Mission Ops";
    )
}

/** A ground station / ground segment receiving downlinked products. */
actor def GroundSegment {
    public (
        attribute stationId : String [1];
        attribute bandSupport : String [1] = "X-band";
    )
}

/** Autonomous onboard fault monitor (FDIR) that triggers safe mode. */
actor def FaultMonitor {
    public (
        attribute scope : String [1] = "onboard FDIR";
        attribute latching : Boolean [1] = true;
    )
}
